   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Not sure why you are using the weird, unnecessary piping operator from the Hadley-Wickham-verse, but it seems you are using it incorrectly.  The call is passing your model to the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> data= </font>argument.  I assume <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">jes3A_D</font> is your <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">data.frame</font>?  Try following the format shown by the developer in the lavaan tutorial:<div><br></div><div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">crossA_D </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model_jes3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> jes3A_D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ordered </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;PARTY1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ELECTION1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;CONGRESS1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;INFLU1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;COMPLEX1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;NOCARE1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;PARTY2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ELECTION2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;CONGRESS2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;INFLU2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;COMPLEX2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;NOCARE2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div><i><br></i></div><div><a href=\"https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420672305000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1V_1TbYmRkIiOBDLZHW-QC\">https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/index.html</a><br></div><div><i><br></i></div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420672305000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1YrJns8_wZnU665VN5hPhy\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div><div></div></div></div>"
